    "done_when": "Write the record of the resolution-pivot assessment as docs/research/resolution-pivot-assessment.html, a reckon research document with plan-informs converged-forward-solve and plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve. It must read on its own for someone who missed the session.\n\nSources: the eight reports under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/resolution-pivot/ (pivot-census, pivot-gpucost, pivot-archaeology, pivot-critique, proto-ladder, proto-order2, proto-taylor, proto-support), their row receipts in the run directories those reports cite, and the resolution-strategy decision on the plan.\n\nDone when:\n(1) The document states the lead's question, the verdict (accuracy failure came from support, not resolution; the saddle normal form is needed at any resolution; compile cost is flat in cell count and comes from the kernel point jet; refinement converges once the support is right) and the decision, each claim with its number, job id and report.\n(2) It includes three figures under docs/figures/resolution-pivot/, one SVG each, drawn with matplotlib on the data-ink style (plt.style.use(\"data-ink\"); no grid, no title, despined, direct labels; sizes and colour rules as in the global agent guidelines):\n- certificate map relative sup against realised cells, log-log, for the legacy and exact supports in the diverted and limited cases, with the exact arm's booking and exterior terms dashed and the 0.01 bound dotted grey;\n- the topology read's diverted saddle membership error against cells for the current read and the quadratic-only arm, with the bound as a dotted line and the lost X-point at 2,000 cells marked;\n- the kernel-backed read's expanded equations by call site, native against batched, with the cold compile walls labelled.\n(3) Every number in a figure is read from a receipt file, never typed in, and the plotting script is committed under scripts/prototypes/pivot_figures.py.\n(4) It ends with a table of the six blockers, each mapped to its followup id.\n(5) reckon audit-doc reports 0 errors, figures use project-absolute src (/nova/figures/resolution-pivot/...), and filepath relativize is run over the document before committing. Plotting is light work and may run in place on the fleet allocation with the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python and PYTHONPATH set to the worktree. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies; the manifest commits line lists every commit; status is complete, blocked or failed.",
